From: Ruhan van der Berg <35257374+RuhanSA079@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 22:20:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] soc: rapuyama: videocore: quiet the 10 s frame stats

The "N frames in 10 s" line is printed unconditionally, so it keeps
filling the kernel ring buffer long after the display is known to work
and pushes out anything older (it is why the uart probe lines had
scrolled away by the time bluetooth was being debugged). Put it behind
the existing debug parameter; the counters still run, so turning debug
back on at runtime starts reporting again.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/soc/rapuyama/videocore.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/soc/rapuyama/videocore.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/rapuyama/videocore.c
@@ -2405,7 +2405,8 @@
 						    "brightness: %d\n", ret);
 		}
 		if (time_after(jiffies, vc->st_next)) {
-			if (vc->st_frames)
+			/* the counters keep running, only the line is noise */
+			if (debug && vc->st_frames)
 				dev_info(vc->dev, "%u frames in 10 s (%s): push avg %llu us, max %llu us, avg %u rows\n",
 					 vc->st_frames, vc->dma_ok ? "dma" : "pio",
 					 div_u64(vc->st_ns, vc->st_frames * 1000),
-- 
2.43.0

